'''Pokémon: Mega Evolution Special''' (Japanese: '''ポケットモンスターXY特別編 最強メガシンカ''' ''Pocket Monsters XY Special Episode: The Strongest Mega Evolution'') is a series of four special episodes of ''[[Pokémon the Series: XY]]'' that are set during {{Ash}}'s {{pkmn|journey}} through [[Kalos]]. The specials focus on an original protagonist and former [[Professor's assistant|assistant]] of {{an|Professor Sycamore}}, [[Alain]], and his partner, a Mega {{TP|Alain|Charizard}} X, and his quest to research and defeat every known [[Mega Evolution|Mega-Evolved Pokémon]]. He is joined by [[Mairin]], a beginning {{pkmn|Trainer}} who [[First partner Pokémon|started]] with her {{p|Chespin}}, [[nickname]]d [[Chespie]]. Other characters include {{Steven}}, the [[Hoenn League]] {{pkmn|Champion}}, and [[Lysandre]], a mysterious benefactor who has his own reasons for pursuing Mega Evolution.

In Japan, the first special aired on April 3, 2014, a week after the Japanese debut of ''[[XY021|A PokéVision of Things to Come!]]''. It focused on Alain's journey to different parts of Kalos to fight and defeat Trainers with Mega Pokémon, including [[Siebold]] of the Kalos [[Elite Four]]. Subsequent episodes aired in Japan on a biyearly basis, with the second and third episodes focusing around Mega {{p|Rayquaza}}, the [[Primal Reversion|Primal forms]] of {{p|Groudon}} and {{p|Kyogre}}, and the origins of Mega Evolution in Hoenn. The fourth and final special aired on October 29, 2015, tying directly into the ''XY&Z'' arc of ''[[Pokémon the Series: XY]]''.

In the United States, the first special aired on May 31, 2014, a week after the English debut of ''[[XY019|A Conspiracy to Conquer!]]''. The remaining three specials aired before the [[XY050|first episode]] of, halfway through, and the week after the [[XY093|last episode]] of [[S18|Pokémon the Series: XY Kalos Quest]].

